[al:新概念英语（一）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:A Walk Through the Woods]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]

[00:00.95]Lesson 143 | 第143课
[00:03.87]A walk through the woods | 穿越树林的散步
[00:07.33]Listen to the tape then answer this question. | 听录音,然后回答这个问题。
[00:12.86]What was so funny about the words on the sign? | 标牌上的字有什么可笑的?
[00:19.84]I live in a very old town which is surrounded by beautiful woods. | 我住在一个非常古老的城镇,周围是美丽的树林。
[00:28.00]It is a famous beauty spot. | 它是一个著名的风景胜地。
[00:32.06]On Sundays, hundreds of people come from the city to see our town and to walk through the woods. | 星期天,数百人从城市来参观我们的城镇,在树林里散步。
[00:42.50]Visitors have been asked to keep the woods clean and tidy. | 游客们被要求保持树林的整洁。
[00:49.55]Litter baskets have been placed under the trees, but people still throw their rubbish everywhere. | 树下放着垃圾篓,但人们仍然到处乱扔垃圾。
[00:58.99]Last Wednesday, I went for a walk in the woods. | 上星期三,我去树林里散步。
[01:05.51]What I saw made me very sad. | 我所看到的让我非常伤心。
[01:10.74]I counted seven old cars and three old refrigerators. | 我数了七辆旧汽车和三台旧冰箱。
[01:18.12]The little baskets were empty and the ground was covered with pieces of paper, | 小篮子都是空的,地上铺满了纸屑,
[01:25.80]cigarette ends, old tyres, empty bottles and rusty tins. | 烟头、旧轮胎、空瓶子和生锈的罐子。
[01:34.49]Among the rubbish, I found a sign which said, 'Anyone who leaves litter in these woods will be prosecuted!' | 在垃圾中,我发现了一个牌子,上面写着:'任何在这些树林里乱扔垃圾的人将被起诉!'